# Interactive mass-envelope gate for licensed BADA 4.2 A320-232 data.
# Run from BlueSky with: IC research/pybada-envelope-mass
00:00:00.00>ECHO === PYBADATEM MASS ENVELOPE INTERACTIVE GATE ===
00:00:00.10>PLUGIN LOAD PYBADATEM
00:00:00.20>PLUGIN LOAD RESEARCHRECORDER
00:00:00.30>PERFMODEL BADA4
00:00:01.00>CRE MASSR,A320-232,41.30,2.10,90,FL100,250
00:00:01.10>CRE MASSE,A320-232,41.32,2.10,90,FL100,250
00:00:02.00>ENVELOPECHECKS MASSR CUSTOM MASS_MIN MASS_MAX
00:00:02.10>ENVELOPECHECKS MASSE CUSTOM MASS_MIN MASS_MAX
00:00:03.00>RECORDRESEARCH START pybada-envelope-mass.csv
# OFF accepts a positive but deliberately impossible mass without BADA checks.
00:00:04.00>MASS MASSR 100000
# Enabling REPORT on the already-infeasible aircraft accepts and reports it.
00:00:05.00>ENVELOPE MASSR REPORT
# ENFORCE is enabled on the second, initially feasible aircraft.
00:00:05.10>ENVELOPE MASSE ENFORCE
# Fundamental invalidity is rejected even under an envelope policy.
00:00:06.00>MASS MASSE 0
# Selected-envelope failure is rejected without changing MASSE's mass.
00:00:06.10>MASS MASSE 100000
# Recover MASSR, then recur: REPORT accepts both and emits only on recurrence.
00:00:07.00>MASS MASSR 65000
00:00:08.00>MASS MASSR 100000
00:00:09.00>PERFSTATUS MASSR
00:00:09.10>PERFSTATUS MASSE
00:00:10.00>RECORDRESEARCH STOP
00:00:10.10>ECHO === EXPECT MASSR INFEASIBLE AT 100000 kg ===
00:00:10.20>ECHO === EXPECT MASSE VALID WITH ITS PRESERVED, FUEL-DEPLETED MASS ===
00:00:11.00>HOLD
